00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.480
BETH: What is a Behaviour Support Plan?

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.850
JOE: Well, it is a plan that contains
a range of strategies which not only

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:11.010
focus on the behaviour that challenges of
individuals with autism, but also includes

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:15.079
ways to ensure that they have access
to things that are important to them.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.980
A behaviour support plan is a
document that is created to help

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.959
understand and manage behaviour
in individuals with autism to show

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.160
behaviour that others find challenging.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.780
It provides parents and carers with
a step-by-step guide to make sure the

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.100
individual has a good quality of life.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:36.900
BETH: It also enables parents and carers
to identify when intervention is needed

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.260
to prevent behaviour that challenges
and help with positive reinforcement.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:46.220
A good behaviour support plan is based
on the results of a functional assessment

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.439
and uses a ‘Positive Behaviour Support’,
a holistic approach which considers not

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:55.930
only the behaviour itself, but also the
circumstances and characteristics of the

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:00.450
individual exhibiting the behaviour and
the people and situations surrounding it.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.039
It’s proactive and preventative,
focusing on the teaching of new skills

00:01:05.039 --> 00:01:06.919
to replace behaviours that challenge.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.749
JOE: The plan contains a range of
strategies which not only focus on

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.090
the behaviours but also includes ways
to ensure the person has access to

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.360
things that are important to them.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.639
These strategies used are referred to
as proactive strategies and reactive

00:01:21.639 --> 00:01:25.479
strategies and a good behaviour
support plan has more proactive

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.160
strategies than reactive ones.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.160
Proactive strategies are tools
that are used to prevent or avoid

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.970
problem behaviour from occurring.

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:38.520
They are introduced before any behaviours
that challenge start and help to

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.390
reduce the chances of them occurring.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:44.910
BETH: This helps to ensure that the focus
of the plan is not just on the behaviour

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:49.050
but also provides ways to support
the individual to have a good life,

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.690
enabling them to learn better and more
effective ways of getting what they need.

